                            <p>This attribution was accepted (albeit with a query) in the second
                                edition of Medieval Libraries of Great Britain (1964). However, the
                                attribution was later rejected in the Supplement (1987). The
                                corresponding Medieval Libraries of Great Britain index card records
                                the following information, which was deemed unsatisfactory for an
                                attribution:</p><p>Liturgical details point to an original
                                Augustinian owner in Lincolnshire and the name of <persName>Henricus
                                    Abbas de Brunne</persName> is among s. xiii obits. "About the
                                beginning of the s. xv it passed into Cistercian hands" (compare
                                Catalogue).</p></provenance>
